Port shape of values.bot loop-in-error-propagates (top-level type Small = Int in 0..10 and error TooBig already exist there): block: fn check(n: int) -> Small errors TooBig:
    if n > 10:
        fail TooBig
    elif n < 0:
        fail TooBig
    else:
        n
fn run(k: int) errors TooBig:
    loop i from 0 to 3:
        check(k)
fn outcome(k: int):
    v = run(k):
        on TooBig:
            return "TooBig"
    v
[outcome(20), outcome(2)] -> ["TooBig", [2, 2, 2]] (strict-accepted, verified on interp): the error escapes the whole loop, no partial List

